  "slug": "scientific-fair-5429",
  "summary": "Spatial and time-resolved transcriptomics now enable inference of cell-state dynamics and interaction terms, not only descriptive trajectories.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is inferring dynamical laws of cell behavior from time-resolved or snapshot single-cell and spatial transcriptomics, with explicit representation of interaction terms. A many-body stochastic framework learns cell-cell interaction laws, including nonreciprocal couplings, from experimental multicellular migration trajectories. stMIND uses a continuous-time neural SDE to infer multiscale spatial-temporal interaction dynamics from unmatched time-resolved spatial transcriptomics. CytoBridge reconstructs continuous virtual cell dynamics from spatial snapshots using an unbalanced mean-field Schrödinger bridge. CellVocal integrates spatial RNA velocity with cell-cell communication to attribute cell-state transitions to intrinsic and signalling components. The Fish Metastasis Atlas instead maps organ-specific Ewing sarcoma dissemination in zebrafish, a distinct question from the dynamical inference shared by the others. What is new is the explicit inclusion of signalling and interaction terms within inferred dynamics, rather than their use as descriptive context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-13"
}
